WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.820
- I'm Ragini, a director at Jubilee,

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:10.240
and have been making videos
here for over a year.

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.770
For those who can't tell I'm an Indian.

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:15.170
And in fact, was born and raised in India.

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:17.210
So to bring some shows back to my roots,

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:18.310
I flew to New Delhi

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:21.330
and shot a few episodes with
the help of a great crew.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.763
Very excited to share the first
chapter of Jubilee in India.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.230
- [Pradhyuman] When I'm
speaking to someone I'll open

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:29.110
up layer by layer.

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:31.665
- [Aakanksha] Do you really want to commit

00:00:31.665 --> 00:00:33.240
to a lifetime of staying with someone

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.460
before you've really
discovered all the layers

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:36.293
of the person?

00:00:36.293 --> 00:00:37.462
- Yeah.

00:00:37.462 --> 00:00:38.295
- Because you know, three layers down

00:00:38.295 --> 00:00:41.460
you might realize that, you
found one that's a deal breaker.

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:51.370
- When I started the process

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:54.120
of arranged marriage I was 25

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.910
and when I got married, I was 29

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.910
- Arranged marriage is a beautiful concept

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:01.300
because it just expands your horizons

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.980
to meet more potential people.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:06.070
- I got arranged marriage when I was 21

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:07.440
and I think that was very, very young.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.103
We parted ways because
we grew differently.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.270
- I do agree that arrange
marriages are an entire spectrum

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:17.300
which also do include
marriages, which are autonomous.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.160
And the choice is given
to the bride and groom

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.400
to say no or to say yes,

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:24.630
but by and large, I think
agency is non-existent.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:26.470
- That set up doesn't kind of,

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:27.890
you know, give you the
structure or the framework

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:30.450
to explore the other person's values

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:32.820
and beliefs and priorities.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.930
- So I had a love marriage,
but of course we grew apart,

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.000
but it also gave me a lot

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.370
of insight into my own self.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:40.510
What did I want?

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:42.350
- I really feel it was
one of the most beautiful

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:43.700
relationship I've ever had.

00:01:58.489 --> 00:02:01.730
Hi, I'm Rina, I'm a shoe
designer, a polo player

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:04.610
and a DJ and I'm pro arrangement.

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:05.897
- Hi I'm Pankhuri.

00:02:05.897 --> 00:02:08.650
I'm 35 years old and I'm a makeup artist

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:12.159
and I'm pro arranged marriage.

00:02:12.159 --> 00:02:13.730
- Hi I'm Pradhyuman.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:15.620
I'm 31 years old.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:17.480
I am a jewelry designer.

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:18.690
I'm an entrepreneur

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:21.610
and I was a participant
in Indian matchmaking.

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:23.350
I am pro arranged marriage.

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:24.920
- Hi, I am Aastha.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:26.530
I am 22 years old.

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:29.790
I am an aspiring musician
and I'm also a law student

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:32.153
and I am anti arranged marriage.

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:34.070
- Hi, I'm Aakanksha

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:37.160
I'm 32 years old and I
work for American Express

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:38.710
and I'm anti arranged marriage.

00:02:38.710 --> 00:02:40.166
- I'm Suvir.

00:02:40.166 --> 00:02:41.220
I'm 47.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:42.810
I'm an architect and a trainer

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:44.503
and I'm anti arranged marriage.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:50.933
- [Interviewer] Arranged
marriages are an outdated concept.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:54.590
If you agree, please step forward.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:05.113
- We've evolved.

00:03:05.113 --> 00:03:07.620
The societies have evolved and
there's a lot about freedom

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.480
and expressions and I want
to have those fulfillment.

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:15.070
So I think in today's times,
it has gone out of context.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:18.310
- The aspirations, regardless
of the genders, are changing.

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:20.360
How do you fit into those boxes?

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:22.110
Those, those pigeonholes.

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:26.020
You cannot expect that I
changed my entire sense

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:27.580
of style and my personality,

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:30.530
the way I express myself,
just because I married you.

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:32.930
What the hell is so special about you?

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:36.420
- The gender bias is so,
it's so painfully obvious.

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:39.270
I would never, like,
voluntarily put myself

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:42.380
in a position where some
stranger can just come,

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:46.000
evaluate my character,
my market reputation,

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.820
put me under labels like too dark,

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:50.250
too thin, too fat, whatever.

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.100
And actually I was having
a discussion with my

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:53.160
best friend last night,

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:54.390
I was telling her how excited I am

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:56.660
to be having this conversation today.

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:58.790
And she told me that when she was young,

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:02.510
when she was seven or eight,
she herself was involved

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:05.300
in these potential bride
visits of her uncle.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:08.280
They used to go to some like
perspective bride's house

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:11.980
and not even talk, just observe her.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:14.670
And then in the car ride back home,

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:17.700
entire conversation would
almost always centered only

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:19.330
around her physical attributes.

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:20.350
Her belly was showing,

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:21.710
so there was some stretch marks there.

00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:23.110
And just imagine the kind

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:26.450
of imprint it would have had
on a girl who's just seven.

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:29.120
And she says that she still
carries the insecurities

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.250
that were bred because of that.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.703
- [Interviewer] Can we have
the disagreers come forward?

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:41.100
- Globally arranged marriages is just 60%.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:45.263
In India its still 90%
with 1% divorce rate.

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:48.490
Whereas globally,

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:51.560
I feel like arranged
marriage is not outdated

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.230
but it's growing.

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:55.730
I know because I lived
in New York for 10 years

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:58.330
and my friends wanted their parent

00:04:58.330 --> 00:04:59.320
to get them arranged marriage.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:03.210
And these people are living,
born, brought up in New York.

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:06.180
So I just feel that I
think it's coming back,

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:08.070
much more strongly.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:12.100
I mean just having this
show is a very big sign that

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.260
in this day and age, this show is shown

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:17.800
that even educated people
are asking their parents

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:21.210
because they believe that these
values are also important.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.517
Love alone is not important.

00:05:24.541 --> 00:05:27.280
- Okay, I have been on the
online dating apps as well.

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:29.670
I'm having a great
conversation with this girl.

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:30.740
It's going wonderful.

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:31.573
Wonderful.

00:05:31.573 --> 00:05:34.180
Like soul mate kind of
conversation, right?

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:37.900
One day my data is off I'm in some,

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:39.980
no network zone, okay?

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:41.800
She thinks that, okay, what's happening?

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:44.120
There is no respond to it, like this,

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:46.220
this person is not interested anymore.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:50.140
To continue that conversation ahead, okay?

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:53.340
There was a drop rate of 95%.

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:56.010
After a year, I was like,
listen, I can't give

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:59.780
so much time trying to have
this conversation with someone.

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:01.770
And then suddenly it goes away.

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:03.000
Arranged marriage really helps

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.530
because the person is
constantly obliged, okay?

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:07.830
That speak it through.

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:10.572
When I'm speaking to someone I'll open up

00:06:10.572 --> 00:06:11.490
layer by layer

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:14.390
and that layering takes always some time.

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:17.780
And when you have a support in
terms of someone telling you

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:19.940
and guiding you, it works wonderfully.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:21.196
- I have a question for you.

00:06:21.196 --> 00:06:22.029
- So I want to add-

00:06:22.029 --> 00:06:23.710
- [Aakanksha] Just a question to him.

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:25.690
Do you really want to commit

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:27.890
to a lifetime of staying with someone

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:31.140
before you really discovered
all the layers of the person?

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:33.610
Because you know, three layers down,

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:35.560
that you found a layer
that's a deal breaker.

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:37.580
- Yes, but even after a love marriage

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:40.900
you will find layers,
which are always opening up

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:44.110
- The essence I think people
have lost it over the period

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:44.943
of time.

00:06:44.943 --> 00:06:47.480
It was a beautiful thing that
two unknown people were made

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:50.630
to meet one another through
common friends and family.

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:54.030
And if you liked each other,
you continued the process.

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:54.890
So that's the thing,

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:57.600
It depends on how your family
also portrays it to you.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:00.400
I was never pushed to go and
meet a guy if I didn't like.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.810
So that thing I think,
and that is very liberal.

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:05.490
I think the basic sense and the portrayal

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:07.120
of arranged marriage should not be like,

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:08.780
Oh no if I'm going to meet this guy,

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:10.690
my parents are going to tell me-

00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:11.930
(Talking over each other)

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:13.330
- Since you used the word liberal,

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:16.160
I just want to say that historically a lot

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:19.710
of arranged marriages
were arranged by elders,

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:20.720
so that the caste status

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:22.220
of the families could be maintained.

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:24.370
- Yeah of course, that still
happens in outside Delhi.

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:25.320
When you cross the borders

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:27.000
of Delhi it still happens.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.500
- Its more like an arranged love marriage.

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:30.330
- It's not the pressure
of getting married.

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:31.920
It's the pressure that, you know what,

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:33.630
the environment I'm
meeting this person for

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:37.780
in the first time is not a
natural environment for me.

00:07:37.780 --> 00:07:38.613
Right?

00:07:38.613 --> 00:07:40.400
The guy's family is there.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:41.470
My family is there.

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:45.800
I am decked up like a doll,
which I am generally not, and-

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:47.800
- But you're doing it with your own wish.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:50.860
- I think a sense of agency
and choices is very loosely

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:51.910
and it doesn't actually exist.

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:54.020
- I being 46, I have a lot of nieces

00:07:54.020 --> 00:07:57.150
and nephews and I, being
a DJ or a polo player,

00:07:57.150 --> 00:08:00.900
I come across 25 to 35 where a lot

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:02.200
of people want to get married.

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:04.710
And what I see through, these apps,

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:06.330
they're breaking their hearts.

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:10.540
They're lying, it's constant
lying, it's constant hooking up.

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:12.080
It's constant this is going on.

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:13.900
They come back, their heart is broken,

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:15.010
they are in depression.

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:17.090
But, what I'm saying is why
arranged marriage is coming

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:19.340
because after your heart
is broken over these apps,

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:21.010
once, twice, thrice,

00:08:21.010 --> 00:08:23.720
you confide that your
parents are not going

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:27.280
to force you but at
least do a little check

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:30.280
of that person and that
family background instead

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:32.540
of this app where people are lying

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:33.940
and I have also been on that app.

00:08:35.350 --> 00:08:37.650
So to be very honest, I'm the only one

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:40.980
in my family or friends to
have had arranged marriage.

00:08:40.980 --> 00:08:42.610
My experience with the
arranged marriage is

00:08:42.610 --> 00:08:47.150
that it was a very exciting
period, we became friends,

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:50.270
we got to know each other ,
our families knew each other.

00:08:50.270 --> 00:08:52.240
The culture was similar.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:54.310
- So there has been a
mix of arranged marriages

00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:57.410
and love marriages in my
friends and my family,

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:58.880
most have been an arranged marriages,

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:01.160
and by God's grace all

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:02.860
of them have been doing very well.

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:07.110
- [Interviewer] Arranged
marriages perpetuate religious

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:08.833
and caste divisions.

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:15.560
- Obviously I talk about this whole thing

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:17.190
with my family members a lot also.

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:21.290
And I was talking about how
autonomy is so important to me

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:23.640
and I will only marry a
person of my own choice.

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:25.499
And they said that

00:09:25.499 --> 00:09:27.690
(speaking foreign language)

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:29.110
What is that supposed to mean?

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:30.510
I mean, why do honor killings happen?

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:32.010
So yes, I do believe that they definitely

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:35.490
perpetuate caste divisions,
religious divisions.

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:39.330
- So my personal experience is my husband,

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:40.680
he's from a Sikh family.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:43.830
My father-in-law ties a turban
and they go to the Gurudwara.

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:46.861
So my thoughts were this
only that, you know,

00:09:46.861 --> 00:09:50.200
arranged marriage will
have you divided into caste

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:52.540
and, you know, have you coming
from different communities

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:54.350
and I will have different ways,

00:09:54.350 --> 00:09:56.330
religious expectations and all.

00:09:56.330 --> 00:09:58.077
But when I got married to my husband

00:09:58.077 --> 00:09:59.650
and we had an arranged marriage,

00:09:59.650 --> 00:10:01.400
till date, never,

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:04.360
they have never asked me to understand or

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:06.750
to start learning their language.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:09.640
If the families and
everybody is liberal and open

00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:12.010
about it you can have
inter-caste marriages,

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:13.330
and they are successful

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:21.330
- To make my stand clear, I
am pro inter-caste marriages.

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:22.300
If you meet the right person

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:24.930
at the right place at the right time.

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:29.930
My only thing is that
the human nature feeds

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.170
on familiarity.

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:33.100
Today, I'm traveling, I see an Indian.

00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:35.980
We automatically become friends, right?

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:38.840
The concept of arranged marriage is

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:42.860
to meet the people whom
you're familiar with, right?

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:45.450
And in most cases, the
familiar people are people

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:49.020
of the same societies,
from the same caste.

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:51.330
So that is the reason I don't see it

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:54.950
as actually perpetuating religious divide.

00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:57.280
I see it that because people are familiar,

00:10:57.280 --> 00:10:59.720
that is when like, you know,
it's going to be easier.

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:03.150
- Like, I'll just say
that recently I have a lot

00:11:03.150 --> 00:11:05.300
of younger friends in America

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:08.760
and their parents are also believing now,

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:11.470
have changed over time and said,

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:14.260
have introducing by
arranged, different caste.

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:15.340
like the Gujurati

00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:19.710
his mother is introducing
her to a known Punjabi.

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:21.960
So things are changing in arranged too.

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:23.153
- 10 years before

00:11:24.284 --> 00:11:25.624
I told my dad, you know,

00:11:25.624 --> 00:11:27.540
that if I like a Muslim
girl, what's going to happen.

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:30.290
Like, it's like, there's no way

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:32.810
you know how dads are like, you know,

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:35.360
you should know where the whole
family is and this and that.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:38.320
10 years down the line he
shows me a girl who's Muslim.

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:39.230
Like, you know what?

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:40.390
I would really love you, if you,

00:11:40.390 --> 00:11:42.320
if you say yes to something like that.

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:43.153
So things change.

00:11:43.153 --> 00:11:44.380
- I have a question for both of you,

00:11:44.380 --> 00:11:46.890
don't you think that
these personal instances,

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:48.100
that you just talked about,

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:51.840
are coming from a place of very high level

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:53.530
of privilege and very disconnected

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:55.250
from how things actually happen in India.

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:57.400
- No India, so I'll tell
you, India I'll tell you.

00:11:57.400 --> 00:12:01.010
I mean it's happening here
as he said his own example.

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:03.810
My, my cousins and their family,

00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:05.970
also, we are Gujurati conservative family.

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:09.080
They are showing their
children now, Punjabi boys.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:11.280
I mean, not Muslim yet but I'm just sayin-

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:13.260
- Are you open to considering
that you guys are exceptions

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:14.850
and this is not the norm.

00:12:14.850 --> 00:12:15.820
- No, no.

00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:18.950
Arranged marriages simply
getting two known people together

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:20.740
whom you can vouch for.

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:22.170
So it can be of one caste

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:23.410
or it can be off any other caste.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:24.360
It does not matter.

00:12:26.380 --> 00:12:29.350
- Someone I know very closely
had her marriage arranged.

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:32.110
So her parents were in a
hurry to get her married.

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:35.040
This guy was set to have a job in a bank.

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:37.340
Now, once they actually got married,

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:40.230
turned out that he didn't
really have that bank job.

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:42.000
He was unemployed, actually.

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:43.160
I think when they started running out

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:44.770
of funds the first thing that he did,

00:12:44.770 --> 00:12:46.380
was he sold off his vehicle.

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:49.120
The next thing that he did was
he sold off his wedding ring.

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:50.600
When she told her parents instead

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:51.790
of taking the responsibility,

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.390
they said that you should just compromise,

00:12:53.390 --> 00:12:55.160
which just made me think that,

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:57.667
that person wasn't there to
find the right partnership

00:12:57.667 --> 00:13:01.210
but it was to reduce that
financial liability on the family.

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:03.030
- [Interviewer] Parental
support is pivotal

00:13:03.030 --> 00:13:04.653
for a successful marriage.

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:14.470
- From my personal experience,
when I got married,

00:13:14.470 --> 00:13:16.010
I had a lot of adjustment issues

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:20.620
with my in-laws or my husband
would not understand my agony.

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:21.760
So then I had to go

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:24.410
and call my mom and ask a lot of advice

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:26.320
even when I had a fall
out with my husband.

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:28.190
And, you know, there
were certain problems.

00:13:28.190 --> 00:13:30.540
I, my mother always
told me that, you know,

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:31.540
I have your back.

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:33.320
You can come back to me anytime.

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:35.320
And she always told me that we are there

00:13:35.320 --> 00:13:36.590
with you no matter what.

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:40.130
And which I think that all
parents are always there

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:42.020
and I feel it's very important.

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:43.810
- I actually agree to what you're saying.

00:13:43.810 --> 00:13:44.960
Me and my husband,

00:13:44.960 --> 00:13:47.470
we met through a friend and
ours is a love marriage.

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:51.360
And, for us, when our families
met they didn't really

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:53.210
like each other so much,

00:13:53.210 --> 00:13:55.420
but his family never
had a problem with me.

00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:58.491
And my family never
had a problem with him.

00:13:58.491 --> 00:14:03.450
And they've been rock solid
support for me and my husband.

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:05.080
My father-in-law has always, you know,

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:06.770
built me up.

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:07.990
If me and my husband fight

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:10.370
and my father-in-law finds out about it,

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:12.303
he's probably going to side with me.

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:15.600
and my father he sees my husband

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:18.640
like a second son and it
makes life so much easier.

00:14:18.640 --> 00:14:22.770
- In my opinion, it's always
a good point to, you know,

00:14:22.770 --> 00:14:26.860
at least have your family as
the team to make a decision.

00:14:26.860 --> 00:14:29.327
They're always going to wish well for you.

00:14:29.327 --> 00:14:31.450
You sit down and explain
that I really love her,

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:33.470
I really want to be with her.

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:36.400
And you know, I will see
myself happy with her

00:14:36.400 --> 00:14:39.300
and I'm sure that other people,

00:14:39.300 --> 00:14:40.610
maybe the first time they disagree,

00:14:40.610 --> 00:14:42.240
but over the time if

00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:44.530
they see that you persistent, it works.

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:47.130
- My parents have been my best
friends since age of five,

00:14:47.130 --> 00:14:48.840
you know, there's
nothing that I don't talk

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:50.200
to her even today.

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:51.200
You know what I mean?

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:53.535
If any problem would
happen I would call her up

00:14:53.535 --> 00:14:54.550
and say mom, now this happened.

00:14:54.550 --> 00:14:57.163
Or mom, what do I do with this?

00:14:58.820 --> 00:15:01.700
- I'm not denying that what they're saying

00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:03.070
but parent support is always there.

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:04.880
Why are you narrowing down
your parents when it comes

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:05.980
to your relationship?

00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:08.300
I want to love somebody
because I love that person.

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:10.450
I want to raise my own family.

00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:12.650
Unless my parents have raised me wrong,

00:15:12.650 --> 00:15:13.930
Why will I make a decision-

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:15.280
No, you let me complete please, sorry.

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:17.111
You've not let me complete.

00:15:17.111 --> 00:15:18.011
(laughing)

00:15:18.011 --> 00:15:19.560
Unless I have been raised

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:21.710
in a wrong way, why
would I choose somebody

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:24.730
or be with somebody who will
not have the same values as me?

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:26.580
I'm going to be with my
partner for a longer time

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:29.620
than I have been with my
parents since I met my partner.

00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:32.300
So I want to take care of
them for 60 more years.

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:34.580
So I'm thinking that then,
I'm not thinking now.

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:37.020
- Don't you get a little
insensitive towards your parents?

00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:38.040
Maybe they also want

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:40.690
to be a part when you're choosing
your partner, maybe they-

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:41.613
- I'm not denying that.

00:15:41.613 --> 00:15:44.960
- Suppose you have a rift with your spouse

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:46.580
and you're confused.

00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:47.740
And you ask your parent,

00:15:47.740 --> 00:15:49.900
would you ask your
parents for your opinion?

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:51.690
- Why are we placing parental judgment

00:15:51.690 --> 00:15:53.330
on such (indistinctive)

00:15:53.330 --> 00:15:54.163
(All talking over on another)

00:15:54.163 --> 00:15:57.269
- One second, One second,
just one more thing

00:15:57.269 --> 00:15:58.250
One second, one second

00:15:58.250 --> 00:16:00.110
Also, if there is a rift between me

00:16:00.110 --> 00:16:02.030
and my spouse that's
an amazing opportunity

00:16:02.030 --> 00:16:04.810
for me to understand each other and grow.

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:06.900
My parents did have an arranged marriage

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:07.970
and I didn't see any issues.

00:16:07.970 --> 00:16:09.430
We were be brought up very nicely,

00:16:09.430 --> 00:16:11.800
there was no problems in that setup,

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:12.800
but today people are looking

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:15.343
for more freedom for more personal growth.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:18.973
- Marriage is primarily about love.

00:16:25.900 --> 00:16:28.570
- True love means when
you accept your partner

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:32.190
with all his flaws and how you tend to go

00:16:32.190 --> 00:16:34.540
on in life, keeping those things together.

00:16:34.540 --> 00:16:35.930
Because after a particular time

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:37.830
in life it's difficult
for people to change.

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:40.210
So I think love is an overall picture.

00:16:40.210 --> 00:16:41.070
You cannot say that, no

00:16:41.070 --> 00:16:44.210
I want a perfect partner
or I wanted a perfect wife.

00:16:44.210 --> 00:16:47.510
No, I think what makes perfect
is like your imperfection

00:16:47.510 --> 00:16:48.720
someone who accepts you

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:50.710
and that is what I believe is true love.

00:16:50.710 --> 00:16:52.750
- Your children would probably
get married and leave.

00:16:52.750 --> 00:16:55.310
Your friends will have their
own lives and get on with them.

00:16:55.310 --> 00:16:58.310
The one person that you decide
to live your entire life

00:16:58.310 --> 00:16:59.640
with, I think.

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:01.470
I don't think a marriage should be for

00:17:01.470 --> 00:17:02.440
one and one thing alone

00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:04.450
but I do think that love
should definitely be one

00:17:04.450 --> 00:17:05.283
of those things.

00:17:11.435 --> 00:17:12.268
- Because of an arranged marriage

00:17:12.268 --> 00:17:14.550
and I really felt that when
I got married it was not

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:15.383
about love.

00:17:15.383 --> 00:17:17.030
I mean, you can't just
love somebody when you just

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:18.810
meet them once or twice.

00:17:18.810 --> 00:17:20.800
And that's why I feel it's not primarily

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:22.910
about love it's about being friends,

00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:25.580
about knowing each other
and growing to each other

00:17:25.580 --> 00:17:30.450
and I feel in arranged marriage
love grows, eventually.

00:17:30.450 --> 00:17:31.990
So, that's what I think.

00:17:31.990 --> 00:17:34.410
- So, I would slightly
deviate from you there

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:37.730
because, so you said that
arranged marriages are

00:17:37.730 --> 00:17:40.850
about growing together and
growing into love eventually.

00:17:40.850 --> 00:17:44.440
But, I think arranged
marriages are a huge gamble,

00:17:44.440 --> 00:17:45.440
a much bigger gamble

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:47.690
than what a non arranged
marriage might be.

00:17:47.690 --> 00:17:49.207
Cause I have friends whose parents have

00:17:49.207 --> 00:17:51.080
had arranged marriages,

00:17:51.080 --> 00:17:53.730
but there is no love in those marriages.

00:17:53.730 --> 00:17:57.070
Seeing that, I just think
that when the stake is so big,

00:17:57.070 --> 00:17:59.030
not just your own life, but your children.

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:01.100
I think it's a slightly bigger gamble

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:03.530
than I myself would be ready to take.

00:18:03.530 --> 00:18:08.530
- I've met quite a few
people during the last couple

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:10.290
of years.

00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:12.890
And when you ask a girl, right,

00:18:12.890 --> 00:18:14.990
that what are you looking in marriage for?

00:18:15.950 --> 00:18:18.260
First thing is like, trust.

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:22.490
Trust is the primary
thing, always, that trust,

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:25.860
and then obviously there's
love which is built

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:28.490
from trust and that gets started later-

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:30.330
- I'm gonna cut you there

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:33.870
and tell you about a small anecdote, okay?

00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:35.870
My husband and I, we met
through a mutual friend

00:18:35.870 --> 00:18:37.930
and we fell in love and we got married.

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:39.560
But, before that happened,

00:18:39.560 --> 00:18:42.780
my parents introduced
me to multiple prospects

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:47.780
and I trusted their
assessment of this prospect.

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:48.850
And I said, fine.

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:50.940
If you think he's the right match for me,

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:53.530
I will go ahead, get
engaged with this person.

00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:58.530
Twice my engagement was
called off, for silly reasons.

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:01.080
One guy refused to even
tell me a reason why.

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:02.760
He sends me a text at the end of the month

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:04.713
saying the month is over and so are we.

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:08.420
And then when we sat down as
families to talk about it,

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:10.680
he got physical with my father!

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:11.910
Is that fair?

00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:13.770
And is that my father's fault?

00:19:13.770 --> 00:19:16.530
Or can I say that I
refuse to trust my father

00:19:16.530 --> 00:19:17.950
because this has happened.

00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:21.120
So this was one, this was
the second guy, actually.

00:19:21.120 --> 00:19:26.120
The first one my parents
found his matrimonial ad

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:28.200
in a newspaper.

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:31.060
I think two days before the
engagement we get a call

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:32.880
from the elder brother's wife,

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:36.250
and she tells us that
she's filed multiple cases

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:37.610
of Dowdy demands

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:40.010
and domestic violence
against the entire family.

00:19:41.130 --> 00:19:43.200
How do my parents find this out?

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:45.280
We were fortunate we found this out.

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:47.670
- But then that's because
you went through a newspaper.

00:19:47.670 --> 00:19:49.482
It was not like a common-

00:19:49.482 --> 00:19:50.315
- [Suvir] Arranged marriage.

00:19:50.315 --> 00:19:51.541
- Its not, it not like usually-

00:19:51.541 --> 00:19:54.358
(talking over one another)

00:19:54.358 --> 00:19:55.772
- [Rina] Usually an arranged marriage

00:19:55.772 --> 00:19:57.210
happens when you know the other family.

00:19:57.210 --> 00:19:59.020
- But this happens.

00:19:59.020 --> 00:20:00.870
When I came to the age

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:04.370
of getting married the first
attempt was actually going

00:20:04.370 --> 00:20:05.707
through the path of arranged marriages

00:20:05.707 --> 00:20:08.800
and those experiences
were not nice at all.

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:11.630
The one arranged marriage
I've seen the most

00:20:11.630 --> 00:20:13.370
closely is the one of my parents.

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:15.890
And it's not been the smoothest

00:20:15.890 --> 00:20:16.910
of the marriages.

00:20:16.910 --> 00:20:17.770
- What I came

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:21.150
across this process was that
people are very judgmental.

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:23.330
They objectify you as a commodity.

00:20:23.330 --> 00:20:24.520
So I was body shamed,

00:20:24.520 --> 00:20:28.450
I was rejected, but
eventually I did get married.

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:31.130
It was an arranged marriage
and my husband accepted me

00:20:31.130 --> 00:20:32.720
for what I am,

00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:35.020
who I am, irrespective of my weight,

00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:38.700
my caste or my financial background.

00:20:38.700 --> 00:20:40.990
- [Interviewer] I have
always wanted a big,

00:20:40.990 --> 00:20:42.550
fat Indian wedding.

00:20:51.323 --> 00:20:52.540
- At 20, I didn't know better.

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:55.710
I wasn't very exposed,
so of course I wanted

00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:59.110
and I did have, I had like a whole week

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:03.130
of whatever I wanted,
you know, I mean it was.

00:21:03.130 --> 00:21:07.393
And I, because my thought
was that I'm married once

00:21:07.393 --> 00:21:09.093
and I want to do it all.

00:21:10.050 --> 00:21:12.280
Of course, now my thoughts
are completely different.

00:21:12.280 --> 00:21:15.050
And I feel what a waste of money that was

00:21:15.050 --> 00:21:16.520
- Having a big fight wedding

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:18.040
having all the relatives around,

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:19.410
having all the festivities,

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:21.290
having all the Bollywood tamasha.

00:21:21.290 --> 00:21:23.300
I always wanted to be the heroine

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:25.250
because that was my time to shine.

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:27.920
But I did keep it in mind, you know,

00:21:27.920 --> 00:21:29.870
that we don't overspend.

00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:33.130
And I realized also what the period

00:21:33.130 --> 00:21:34.180
of time that, you know, we,

00:21:34.180 --> 00:21:35.840
as girls are more fascinated

00:21:35.840 --> 00:21:39.470
by the idea of the wedding
rather than marriage.

00:21:39.470 --> 00:21:40.303
- I agree.

00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:47.670
- So I can never relate
to a big fat wedding

00:21:47.670 --> 00:21:49.470
because for me I've seen how we,

00:21:49.470 --> 00:21:50.670
as Indians, have grown.

00:21:50.670 --> 00:21:52.550
Earlier there were small
festivals used to be all

00:21:52.550 --> 00:21:54.610
about togetherness, celebrating together.

00:21:54.610 --> 00:21:55.940
That essence has gone.

00:21:55.940 --> 00:21:58.930
In fact, I don't get to
meet my relatives for years.

00:21:58.930 --> 00:22:00.974
Why should they drop in into my marriage?

00:22:00.974 --> 00:22:01.859
I don't understand that.

00:22:01.859 --> 00:22:02.692
(All Laughing)

00:22:02.692 --> 00:22:03.525
I don't understand that.

00:22:03.525 --> 00:22:04.810
Instead, some of my friends

00:22:04.810 --> 00:22:06.560
and from other family people in common,

00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:08.000
people have become so close to me

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:09.420
and they have some common interests

00:22:09.420 --> 00:22:10.400
and we have a great evening.

00:22:10.400 --> 00:22:12.200
So why should they not be involved?

00:22:12.200 --> 00:22:14.510
- I don't like big fat Indian weddings

00:22:14.510 --> 00:22:16.150
because they're breeding grounds

00:22:16.150 --> 00:22:18.226
for further arranged marriages.

00:22:18.226 --> 00:22:20.060
(Everyone laughing)

00:22:20.060 --> 00:22:23.971
All aunties casually scanning you

00:22:23.971 --> 00:22:26.920
and start suddenly making remarks.

00:22:26.920 --> 00:22:29.490
I think I would rather just lay back

00:22:29.490 --> 00:22:32.350
and stay away from all that.

00:22:32.350 --> 00:22:35.080
- [Interviewer] I would get
a divorce if I'm unhappy

00:22:35.080 --> 00:22:36.203
in my marriage.

00:22:44.130 --> 00:22:44.980
- I am divorced.

00:22:44.980 --> 00:22:48.540
So I'm living example of that,

00:22:48.540 --> 00:22:50.220
if I'm not happy, I will,

00:22:50.220 --> 00:22:51.550
because I really believe

00:22:51.550 --> 00:22:55.900
that two people can grow
apart, grow differently.

00:22:55.900 --> 00:22:59.030
And then you definitely
make a choice to be happy

00:22:59.030 --> 00:23:02.063
and cut the chord when
it needs to be gone.

00:23:03.170 --> 00:23:05.870
- So, I've been married for
five and a half years now,

00:23:06.748 --> 00:23:08.700
and first three years of my
married life were way tough.

00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:11.200
And I did reach a point where both

00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:13.380
of us decided to get divorced.

00:23:13.380 --> 00:23:16.770
We lived six months separately,

00:23:16.770 --> 00:23:21.770
but things turned around
and we realized that no,

00:23:21.840 --> 00:23:23.630
you know, we should give it another shot.

00:23:23.630 --> 00:23:26.360
And coming from there, we realized,

00:23:26.360 --> 00:23:29.540
what is that is going
to give us happiness?

00:23:29.540 --> 00:23:31.840
What will make our relationship better?

00:23:31.840 --> 00:23:34.620
So, yes, I did get into a situation,

00:23:34.620 --> 00:23:35.930
but I did not get divorced.

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:39.580
We Mo- I would say crossed that bridge.

00:23:39.580 --> 00:23:42.840
And today I am in a much happier marriage.

00:23:42.840 --> 00:23:47.630
- I think life is about priorities, right?

00:23:47.630 --> 00:23:52.210
And if there comes a point where giving up

00:23:52.210 --> 00:23:56.490
on one of your priorities
literally drains the joy out

00:23:56.490 --> 00:24:00.173
of your then you cannot
make the other person happy.

00:24:01.900 --> 00:24:02.970
Unfortunately,

00:24:02.970 --> 00:24:07.080
my parents don't have the
smoothest of the marriages

00:24:07.080 --> 00:24:11.130
and it's been difficult as their child

00:24:11.130 --> 00:24:13.097
because I can see that
my father is unhappy

00:24:13.097 --> 00:24:14.290
and my mother is unhappy.

00:24:14.290 --> 00:24:17.170
And, and it's not because
either of them are bad people

00:24:17.170 --> 00:24:20.513
it's just because they've
grown in different directions.

00:24:21.410 --> 00:24:23.670
And maybe if they had
separated they would have

00:24:23.670 --> 00:24:24.503
been happier.

00:24:24.503 --> 00:24:25.336
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:24:26.220 --> 00:24:27.900
- I would like to comment on that also

00:24:27.900 --> 00:24:30.783
because I lost my mother two months back.

00:24:33.620 --> 00:24:34.453
Unfortunately,

00:24:34.453 --> 00:24:36.970
when my parents had a very
different marriage life

00:24:36.970 --> 00:24:41.170
and I do believe that had
my mother taken the step

00:24:41.170 --> 00:24:43.350
of divorcing and found her happiness

00:24:43.350 --> 00:24:44.360
and found herself,

00:24:44.360 --> 00:24:45.920
she would have been much more happier.

00:24:45.920 --> 00:24:48.430
And maybe around us right now!

00:24:48.430 --> 00:24:50.240
I believe very strongly that

00:24:50.240 --> 00:24:53.700
if two unhappy people cannot
make a happy life together.

00:24:53.700 --> 00:24:56.100
And to be happy with yourself.

00:24:56.100 --> 00:24:58.760
You can only give happiness
to others, if you are at peace

00:24:58.760 --> 00:25:01.130
with yourself, if you're happy from inside

00:25:01.130 --> 00:25:05.353
- I think that arranged
or not arranged, like,

00:25:06.486 --> 00:25:08.080
we all agreed at one point,

00:25:08.080 --> 00:25:10.090
that is very important to be happy.

00:25:10.090 --> 00:25:11.960
And I think that's the underlying fact.

00:25:11.960 --> 00:25:13.860
Either which way in any relationship,

00:25:13.860 --> 00:25:15.670
whichever way you find it,

00:25:15.670 --> 00:25:17.220
whichever way you have to make it work,

00:25:17.220 --> 00:25:18.053
just be happy.

00:25:18.053 --> 00:25:20.750
And I think that I was so glad
that that time no one said

00:25:20.750 --> 00:25:23.063
that happiness is
something you can discount.

00:25:23.920 --> 00:25:25.463
- [Pradhyuman] It was nice seeing you

00:25:25.463 --> 00:25:27.638
- [Rina] Goodbye, it was
so nice to meet you all.

00:25:27.638 --> 00:25:29.471
- [Aakanksha] Likewise.

